{"team":"MIA","col":"#2CD3C6","identity":"run-heavy","funnel":"balanced-D","plays_pg":59.4,"adot":6.6,"report_html":"<div class=\"report\"><h2>Built to Run</h2><p>Their run game attacks the perimeter \u2014 <strong>35% of carries hit the edge</strong> (league ~25%), an outside-zone lean that rewards speed backs and can boom for chunk gains.</p><h3>The Offensive Blueprint</h3><p>Their backs are a real part of the passing game \u2014 RBs see <strong>24%</strong> of targets (vs ~18%), which props up <strong>De'Von Achane</strong>'s reception floor.</p><p>It's a short, rhythm-based passing game \u2014 aDOT just <strong>6.6</strong> \u2014 that lives on YAC and checkdowns, boosting reception totals over big-play yardage.</p><p>They live in the shotgun (75% of snaps vs ~68%) \u2014 a spread, pass-oriented structure.</p><h3>In the Red Zone</h3><p>Inside the 20 they stay aggressive, throwing <strong>55%</strong> of the time, which puts scoring equity on <strong>Jalen Tolbert</strong>.</p><h2>Defense \u2014 A Balanced Defense</h2><p><strong>Soft against opposing tight ends</strong> \u2014 42 rec yds/game (vs ~35). A rec-yards target.</p><p>They lock down opposing WR2s \u2014 just 30 rec yds/game (vs ~36); fade receiving props there.</p><p>They surrender <strong>119 rushing</strong> and <strong>228 passing</strong> yards per game (league ~120 / ~230). No dominant funnel \u2014 read it matchup by matchup.</p><p>They lock down opposing WR1s \u2014 just 53 rec yds/game (vs ~58); fade receiving props there.</p><p>Broadly a leaky unit \u2014 46% success rate allowed (vs ~44%); points come easy against them.</p><h2>The Betting Angles</h2><p>Bottom line: back <strong>De'Von Achane</strong>'s rushing volume in favored/positive scripts.</p><p><em>Built on 2024\u201325 data; the profile rebuilds through the season as the current staff and roster set their own tendencies.</em></p></div>","depth":{"QB":[{"name":"Malik Willis","slot":"QB1","starter":true,"td":26,"props":{"Comp":17.72,"Att